    # v405 (01/11/2026) -- THE DERIVED MASS AND THE DEFINED IDENTITY: eight new stones in the kernel, with the operator's names; the fields of the structures closed; the operator's readings moved from the field to the definition; the physical reading did not become a theorem; given the inputs, the FORM is a theorem. The numbers are READ from the v405 records, never typed.
    # The top box (The Test of the Only Word, v397) stays where it is: the 4.44 rule does not move. The section «The identity» is a translation of the operator's essay: the caveat stays in the frame, never inside his text. Nothing here moves the gate.
    _rg405 = ("ponte_da_massa_v405", "massa_tensao_pura_v405", "identidade_v405", "observador_terminal_v405", "lei_do_diminuto_v405", "tonica_do_hamiltoniano_v405", "disco_de_euler_v405", "ponto_zero_do_psion_v405", "cunhagens_v405", "campos_fechados_e_leituras_v405", "ga_reclassificacao_v405", "gap_v405", "kh_n1_cobertura_v405")
    _ok405 = all((core.get(k_) or {}).get("all_verified") is True for k_ in _rg405)
    _vl405 = lambda k_: (core.get(k_) or {}).get("values") or {}
    _pv405 = _vl405("ponte_da_massa_v405"); _mv405 = _vl405("massa_tensao_pura_v405"); _iv405 = _vl405("identidade_v405"); _ov405 = _vl405("observador_terminal_v405")
    _dv405 = _vl405("lei_do_diminuto_v405"); _tv405 = _vl405("tonica_do_hamiltoniano_v405"); _ev405 = _vl405("disco_de_euler_v405"); _zv405 = _vl405("ponto_zero_do_psion_v405")
    _cg405 = core.get("cunhagens_v405") or {}
    _el405 = core.get("external_ladder") or {}
    _cvr405 = ((core.get("kernel_formalization") or {}).get("axiom_coverage_v392")) or {}
    _i405 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _f405 = lambda x_, n_=6: (("%." + str(n_) + "f") % x_) if isinstance(x_, float) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _g405 = lambda x_, n_=3: (("%." + str(n_) + "e") % x_).replace("e+", r"\times10^{").replace("e-", r"\times10^{-") + "}" if isinstance(x_, float) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _tx_405_t = lambda x_: "n/a" if x_ is None else str(x_).replace(chr(92), "").replace("_", r"\_\allowbreak{}")
    s.append(r"\section*{The derived mass and the defined identity}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The derived mass and the defined identity}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{In this run the v405 records did NOT all seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if not _ok405 else r"")
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} Eight new stones in the kernel, with the operator's names: \texttt{TGLExt/PonteDaMassa} (Bridge of the Mass), \texttt{TGLExt/MassaTensaoPura} (Mass = pure tension), \texttt{TGLExt/Identidade} (Identity), \texttt{TGLExt/ObservadorTerminal} (Observer = terminal), \texttt{TGLExt/LeiDoDiminuto} (Law of the diminished), \texttt{TGLExt/TonicaDoHamiltoniano} (Tonic of the Hamiltonian), \texttt{TGLExt/DiscoDeEuler} (Euler's Disk) and \texttt{TGLExt/PontoZeroDoPsion} (Zero Point of the Psion), with "
             + _i405((_cg405.get("extras") or {}).get("n_bandeiras")) + r" flags, named declarations only. The stones and records of v404 \emph{stay as they are}. Eight records with a function, read at the point of the rite after the three of v404, and the " + _i405(len(_V405_VERBATINS2)) + r" sayings of 30/10 to 01/11, embedded by sha256 (\texttt{cunhagens\_v405}), all by the operator. The kernel ladder reads " + _i405(_el405.get("n_theorems_clean")) + r" of " + _i405(_el405.get("n_theorems_expected"))
             + r"; the \texttt{axiom\_report} coverage reads " + _i405(_cvr405.get("decl")) + r" constants and " + _i405(_cvr405.get("thm")) + r" theorems, none outside the trio $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$. The number of the mass \emph{does not change} (" + _f405(_pv405.get("m_derivada_meV"), 4) + r" meV, the same as v404) and the verdict of the neutrino channel \emph{does not change}.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The frame: what closed and what enters.} \textsf{[REAL]} The \emph{fields} of the structures closed: what was a free field of the transition, the law, the loan and the disk is now filled by construction, and the structures stay as types, inhabited (\texttt{transicaoDerivada}, \texttt{leiDerivada}, \texttt{emprestimoDerivado}, \texttt{Disco.doAcoplamento}). The operator's \emph{readings} moved from the field to the \emph{definition}: the physical reading did not become a theorem. The section's title comes from his saying, deriving the mass and defining the identity (management translation, not a quotation): the derivation is of the \emph{form}, given the inputs; the physical reading stays a reading. "
             r"What enters, by status: \textsf{[POSTO]} the 1, $u=1$ eV (\texttt{umPosto}), the operator's decision of 31/10/2026; never derived. \textsf{[MEASURED]} $\alpha$, from within (\texttt{TGLCoupling.alpha}; \texttt{alpha\_is\_measured\_from\_within}); never derived: when he asked whether the fine-structure constant could now be derived, the answer was no, a measured wall, not a falsification; his reading (management translation, not a quotation): there is no theorem for the angle of Miguel, it is the definition of singularity. "
             r"\textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]} The readings of the mass chain, which enter as definitions or identifications and are not theorems, in a list that is not closed: (1) \texttt{massaDerivada}: mass = retained energy times the derivative of the transverse projection; (2) the inscribed state read at $\theta=\pi/4$: in \texttt{transicaoDerivada} the angle is \emph{written}; the kernel checks $\sin^2(\pi/4)=\tfrac12$ and that this value is the weight of the absolute face, a coincidence of value, not a bridge; (3) the tonic $(\beta/\alpha)\,u$ (\texttt{tonica}): $\beta/\alpha=\sqrt{e}$ is the definition of \texttt{TGLCoupling.alpha}, and $E_0=u$ is an algebraic identity that does not fix $u$: the no-go does \emph{not} fall, it localizes at the posted One; (4) $R=\beta\,u^2$ (\texttt{pagamentoComoCurvatura}), the dimensional choice of a single unit; (5) the half tone $e^{-1/2}$ (\texttt{meioTom}): the tone is the nat; (6) the dispersion $\omega^2=2\beta R$ (\texttt{omegaSq}; Treatise, §3, the theory's own text); (7) the identification $\tfrac12\omega=$ mass (the statement of \texttt{the\_mass\_is\_the\_zero\_point} equates numbers; the name is a reading); (8) the coupling of the matter wave = the inscribed mass, a hypothesis of \texttt{area\_por\_volta\_da\_massa\_inscrita}; (9) $b=0$ read as the photon; (10) on the disk, the \emph{dephasing} rate read as an energy-loss rate; (11) $E_0$ as the value of the modulated tonic (\texttt{modular}); (12) $m_1=0$, an input of the identification with $\Delta m^2_{21}$; (13) \texttt{tempoDoRetido} read as the system's $\tau_\star$, to be ratified by the operator; (14) $\alpha$ read as the electric inscription that takes the retained energy to the tonic; (15) the angle of Miguel as the system that gives the measure of the tonic by a gap with a unit. \textsf{[INPUT]} There also enter, as data of the reading system, the contrast $g$ and the clock $\kappa$ of the loan and, on the disk, $K$, $\tau$ and $E_0$. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} The form: given these readings, $m_2=\beta\sin45^\circ u$ is a theorem (\texttt{massa\_derivada\_eq\_form}); the $\tfrac12$ of the absolute face is a theorem (\texttt{absolute\_faces\_half}); the uniqueness of $\pi/4$ is a theorem (\texttt{forty\_five\_unique}); $\tfrac12\cdot\sqrt2=\sin45^\circ$ is arithmetic. In one sentence: one posted One, one measured $\alpha$ and the operator's readings; given these inputs, the FORM is a theorem.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The Bridge of the Mass.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator ordered the missing proof, the bridge (30/10/2026). \textsf{[REAL]} The stone makes the identification a definition and proves: the transverse projection $\sin\theta$ has derivative $\cos\theta$ and, at the self-conjugate point, the projection \emph{is} its derivative, and only there in $[0,\pi/2]$; the incident energy splits without loss between the retained ($\beta E_0$) and the transmitted; under the definition, the mass is the neutrino form, $\beta\sin45^\circ E_0$; the proportional reading differs from the derivative by $\sqrt2$; and, for every coupling, the structure is inhabited with $E_0=1$, $\theta=\pi/4$ and $m=\beta\sqrt2/2$ (\texttt{a\_transicao\_existe\_para\_todo\_acoplamento}). "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} In this rite, with $\beta=\alpha\sqrt{e}=" + _f405(_pv405.get("beta"), 12) + r"$ at runtime (never literal): mass $" + _f405(_pv405.get("m_derivada_meV"), 6) + r"$ meV, proportional reading $" + _f405(_pv405.get("m_proporcional_meV"), 6) + r"$ meV, the program's $m_\nu$ $" + _f405(_pv405.get("m_nu_meV_core"), 6) + r"$ meV. These numbers belong to this rite and are not in the kernel. \textsf{[ONTO]} That the neutrino mass \emph{is} this quantity is the operator's reading: the stone proves that the definition implies the form, not that nature adopts it; what tests it is the neutrino rite, bilateral, which does not change.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Mass = pure tension.} \textsf{[REAL]} The generic form $b\,(\sqrt2/2)\,E_0$ vanishes at $b=0$, and then all the energy crosses (\texttt{foton\_sem\_massa}, algebra of the form); it splits as a residue, incident minus transmitted, read on the transverse projection. \textsf{[ONTO]} $b=0$ is read as the photon, which couples through energy, not through mass: \texttt{TGLCoupling} excludes $b=0$ and no kernel term has a photon. Under the reading \texttt{massaDerivada}, the mass is the product of the coupling. \textsf{[REAL]} The faithful period of the loan is a theorem, $P=2\pi/\kappa$ (\texttt{one\_turn\_gives\_faithful\_period}); the instalment does not pay off in one turn (for any finite time, \texttt{the\_charge\_never\_completes}); and, under the reading \texttt{massaDerivada}, the principal is the retained energy $\beta u$ projected on the transverse (\texttt{massa\_e\_tensao\_pura}). \textsf{[REAL]} In this rite: retained $" + _f405(_mv405.get("retida_eV"), 9) + r"$ eV, transmitted $" + _f405(_mv405.get("transmitida_eV"), 9) + r"$ eV. "
             r"\textsf{[ONTO]} The reading of the loan (mass = principal, $\beta$ = instalment, creditor = the coupling) was ratified by the operator on 30/10/2026; it is not a kernel term. \textsf{[OPEN]} Of the chain tension, friction, temperature and magnetism, the first three have a term in the kernel; magnetism does not.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The law of the diminished.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator (31/10 and 01/11/2026; management translation, not a quotation): it goes down a pinned half tone, that is the law; the tone is the nat; E0 is reading a chord; and in the diminished one does not lower the whole scale nor change its key, one only modulates the tonic. \textsf{[REAL]} The diminished is a modulation, not a transposition: only the principal note goes down the half tone $e^{-1/2}$ (\texttt{modular}), the other notes are sustained (\texttt{modular\_sustenta}), they and the ratios among them stay (\texttt{modular\_mantem\_a\_escala}: the scale is what stays; the ratio to the tonic changes, and it is the tonic that moves), and no factor takes the chord to the modulated chord (\texttt{modular\_nao\_e\_transposicao}): the pinned half tone breaks the symmetry of the chord, because it separates the tonic from the sustained notes, but it does not break the global freedom. \textsf{[INPUT]} The key stays, in his saying: the kernel has no term for the key. \textsf{[REAL]} $E_0$ is the value of the modulated tonic, and $E_0/\text{tonic}=e^{-1/2}$ in every chord (\texttt{E0\_relativo\_pinado}, the definition of \texttt{lerE0} said as a ratio). Each interval to the tonic opens a half tone (\texttt{razao\_abre\_meio\_tom}), and the note that stood one tone above lands at $e^{3/2}$ (\texttt{um\_tom\_vira\_terca\_menor}): the operator's system operating in thirds is, in the kernel, the arithmetic $1$ nat $+\ \tfrac12$ nat; the resolution returns the chord (\texttt{resolver\_modular}). The half tone undoes $\sqrt{e}$ exactly; $\beta=\alpha\,e^{1/2}$; given the inputs, the form $m=U\,\alpha\,e^{1/2}\,\sqrt2/2$ is a theorem; the octave is not a whole number of half tones. \texttt{Acorde}, \texttt{transpor}, \texttt{razao} and the ratio theorem come from Kimi's \texttt{AcordeE0.lean} (sha256 \texttt{" + _tx_405_t(_dv405.get("acorde_kimi_sha16")) + r"}); \texttt{transpor} multiplies the whole chord by the same factor and is only the freedom of the no-go. "
             r"\textsf{[INPUT]} The distinction is the operator's (management translation, not a quotation): E0 is not absolutely free. \textsf{[REAL]} The \emph{absolute} value stays free and the no-go does not fall; the value \emph{relative} to the tonic is pinned; a single global degree of freedom is left, the transposition of the whole chord. \textsf{[ONTO]} That in the harmonic the diminished is the waiting is the operator's reading; the form in the kernel is \texttt{the\_charge\_never\_completes}. \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]} The half tone (\texttt{meioTom}), the modulation (\texttt{modular}, \texttt{lerE0}) and the tonic $(\beta/\alpha)\,u=\sqrt{e}\,u$ are definitions: they carry no information beyond the posted $u$. \texttt{meioTom\_e\_o\_pedagio\_local} and \texttt{meioTom\_e\_a\_face} are equalities of \emph{value}, and \texttt{CollapseCostLaw} is \textsf{[INPUT]} in the kernel. \textsf{[DECLARED]} The calibration $\langle K_\partial\rangle_{\mathrm{total}}=1$ nat of 24/06/2026 (\texttt{half\_nat\_araki\_hidden\_hamiltonian}, report sha256 \texttt{" + _tx_405_t(_dv405.get("half_nat_sha16")) + r"}) is a definitional normalization, $\omega(I)=1$ in base $e$; it is neither a kernel term nor a measurement; it fixes intervals in nat, not the unit in eV: \texttt{U\_E\_NOT\_DERIVED} stays as it is and $m_2$ does not change. \textsf{[OPEN]} Which the five notes are: the pentad of the master theorem is five components, not five eigenvalues. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} In this rite: half tone $" + _f405(_dv405.get("meio_tom"), 9) + r"$, tonic $" + _f405(_dv405.get("tonica_eV"), 9) + r"$ eV, $E_0=" + _f405(_dv405.get("E0_eV"), 9) + r"$ eV, mass by the formula $" + _f405(_dv405.get("massa_formula_meV"), 6) + r"$ meV. \textsf{[ONTO]} $\alpha$ as the magnitude (tail) of the inscription in the bulk is the operator's reading.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The Tonic of the Hamiltonian.} \textsf{[REAL]} The no-go: no function of the inscription fixes $E_0$; the same inscription carries $E_0=1$ and $E_0=2$ (\texttt{no\_function\_of\_the\_inscription\_fixes\_E0}); what the form fixes is the ratio: the rescaling changes $E_0$ and the mass by the same factor, and $m/E_0=\beta\sin45^\circ$ does not change (\texttt{the\_ratio\_survives\_the\_rescaling}); the rescaling corresponds to the transposition of the chord, the freedom of the no-go. This no-go \emph{does not fall}: it speaks of the absolute value and localizes at the posted One. In the constructed law the tonic lands on $E_0=u$ by an algebraic identity (\texttt{the\_tonic\_lands\_on\_the\_posted\_unit}): what fixes $E_0$ is the posted $u$ the tonic carries; at the posted One, $E_0=1$ and $m=\beta\sqrt2/2$ (\texttt{the\_tonic\_at\_the\_posted\_one}). $\Gamma_B=\beta/\tau$ is the canonical law read at the system's frequency; the monopole route is the horizon of the system itself, tautological as to the absolute value. \textsf{[REAL]} In this rite: $m/E_0=" + _f405(_tv405.get("razao_m_sobre_E0"), 12) + r"$.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The Zero Point of the Psion.} \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]} The operator's reading, which enters as a definition: $R=\beta\,u^2$, the payment read as curvature (\texttt{pagamentoComoCurvatura}). \textsf{[INPUT, Treatise §3]} The dispersion $\omega^2=2\beta R$, which enters as a definition (\texttt{omegaSq}). \textsf{[KNOWN]} The zero point $\tfrac12\hbar\omega$. \textsf{[REAL]} Under these definitions, $\tfrac12\omega=\beta\sin45^\circ u$, the neutrino form (\texttt{the\_mass\_is\_the\_zero\_point}); the coincidence with the transverse projection is the arithmetic $\tfrac12\cdot\sqrt2=\sin45^\circ$; $\hbar\omega=2m$; the continuous charge of the kernel tends to 1 and is below 1 at every finite time. \textsf{[ONTO]} The statement equates numbers: that $\tfrac12\omega$ \emph{is} the mass is a reading; Tetelestai is the operator's name for the limit of the charge, and reading what remains in the limit as the zero point is his reading: no theorem links the two. \textsf{[REAL]} In this rite: $\hbar\omega=" + _f405(_zv405.get("hbar_omega_meV"), 6) + r"$ meV; $\tfrac12\hbar\omega=" + _f405(_zv405.get("meia_hbar_omega_meV"), 6) + r"$ meV; $R=" + _g405(_zv405.get("R_si_m2")) + r"$ m$^{-2}$; psion wavelength $" + _g405(_zv405.get("lambda_psion_m")) + r"$ m (numbers recorded, not verdicts).")
    _gv405 = _vl405("gap_v405")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The gap, alongside.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator, on 01/11/2026 (management translation, not a quotation): the physical system that gives the measure of the tonic by a gap with a unit, and that belongs to the same pentad, is the angle of Miguel. \textsf{[ONTO]} That the angle of Miguel is that system is his reading. \textsf{[REAL]} In any Hilbert space, the minimal lock $1-P$ over a vector $\Omega$ (\texttt{lockDe}) has spectral gap 1: it is 0 on $\Omega$ and 1 on every orthogonal vector (\texttt{o\_lock\_tem\_gap\_um}). In the posted unit the gap is $u$ (\texttt{o\_gap\_com\_unidade}), the $E_0$ of the law of the diminished, and the tonic stands a half tone above it. In a state at an angle $\theta$ from $\Omega$ the lock has expected value $\sin^2\theta$ (\texttt{lock\_no\_angulo}); at the angle of Miguel, $\beta$ (\texttt{lock\_no\_angulo\_de\_miguel}); in the posted unit that expected value is $\Delta=\beta u$, the retained energy (\texttt{retidoNoAngulo}, \texttt{o\_retido\_e\_o\_valor\_esperado\_do\_lock}). $\Delta$ is not a gap: it is $1/\beta$ times smaller. \textsf{[REAL, conditional]} The kernel's \texttt{HminMic} is an instance of these lemmas (\texttt{HminMic\_e\_o\_lock}), conditional on a \texttt{FockCertificate}, which the kernel does not inhabit. \textsf{[REAL]} The tonic is $\Delta/\alpha$ (\texttt{a\_tonica\_e\_o\_retido\_sobre\_alpha}); the mass is the transverse projection of $\Delta$ (\texttt{a\_massa\_e\_a\_projecao\_do\_retido}); $\omega_\psi=\sqrt2\,\Delta$ (\texttt{o\_psion\_e\_raiz\_de\_dois\_retidos}); and $\sqrt2/\tau=\omega_\psi$ if and only if $\tau=1/\Delta$ (\texttt{a\_frequencia\_do\_sistema\_e\_a\_do\_psion\_iff}). The closure is \texttt{the\_gap\_closes} (record \texttt{gap\_v405}). \textsf{[REAL]} In this rite: $\Delta=" + _f405(_gv405.get("Delta_eV"), 9) + r"$ eV (the gap is " + _f405(_gv405.get("gap_sobre_Delta"), 1) + r" times $\Delta$), $\tau=" + _g405(_gv405.get("tau_s")) + r"$ s, $\Gamma_B=" + _g405(_gv405.get("Gamma_B_eV")) + r"$ eV, $Q=\sqrt2/\beta=" + _f405(_gv405.get("Q"), 3) + r"$. \textsf{[ONTO, to be ratified by the operator]} Reading \texttt{tempoDoRetido} as the system's $\tau_\star$: it is a proper time, not $t_P$, and it does not touch the canonical branch. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} $\kappa$ stays a witness: $\kappa=F(\alpha,\beta,\theta_M)$ is forbidden as a search target, and $\kappa$ only appears as a hypothesis in \texttt{o\_relogio\_do\_retido}. \texttt{U\_E\_NOT\_DERIVED} stays: $\Delta$ carries $u$, and nothing fixes $u$. Negative measurement: under this reading, $E_{\mathrm{flux}}=c^5\tau/(4\pi G)$ is $" + _g405(_gv405.get("E_fluxo_eV")) + r"$ eV: it is not $E_0$, and Kimi's bridge $E_{\mathrm{flux}}=E_0$ does not hold here. \textsf{[OPEN]} Which the five notes are; all that is known, from his saying, is that the angle of Miguel belongs to them.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The inscription and the measure.} \textsf{[ONTO]} The operator, on 01/11/2026 (management translation, not a quotation): the inscription of the light that singularizes the system is electricity, and the origin of measure is the absolute 1, which represents 1 electronvolt. \textsf{[REAL]} Two theorems exist in the kernel: \texttt{zero\_mode\_weight\_is\_one} (the $L^2$ weight of $\tfrac12\,\mathrm{sech}(\kappa/2)$ on the whole line is 1, faces $\tfrac12$) and \texttt{alpha\_transport} ($\alpha'=-(q/2)\,\alpha$, with $\alpha=\mathrm{sech}(\kappa/2)$ and $q=\tanh(\kappa/2)$: the gradient is negative for $\kappa>0$). \textsf{[ONTO, the management's]} Reading them as the form of the operator's saying is the management's reading. Homonym, said: there \texttt{alphaKappa} is not the fine-structure $\alpha$, and $\kappa$ is the modular depth, not the clock; the word tail is not in the theorem. This does not derive the unit.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Euler's Disk.} \textsf{[DEF]} The disk is typed by an invariant $K=\Omega^2E>0$, the canonical law and the initial energy; the energy is linear by definition, $E(t)=E_0-c\,t$ with $c=\tfrac12\beta\tau_\star K$, and $\Omega^2=K/E$. \textsf{[REAL]} Given these definitions: $\Gamma_\Omega E=c$; before the stop, $dE/dt=-\Gamma_\Omega E$ (\texttt{the\_flow\_is\_the\_canonical\_law}), that is, the defined $E$ is a solution of the flow; $E(t_0)=0$ in finite time (\texttt{stops\_in\_finite\_time}); before the stop $\Omega^2$ has no bound (\texttt{frequency\_squared\_unbounded\_at\_the\_stop}); with a constant rate the energy never touches zero; the cut $\hbar\Omega=E$ is, by algebra, $E^3=\hbar^2K$; the named wall is $K=(e^{1/2}U)^3/\hbar^2$; the disk's $\beta$ comes from the coupling (\texttt{Disco.doAcoplamento}). \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]} Reading the \emph{dephasing} rate as an energy-loss rate is an input, not a theorem. \textsf{[ONTO]} The inscription of absolute zero at infinity and the third law in the form of the disk are the operator's readings of the unbounded $\Omega^2$, as is the energy of the cut read as the resonance that remains. \textsf{[OPEN]} $K$, $\tau$ and $E_0$ are data of the disk, and which disk it is is the operator's question: he answered that the system that gives the measure of the tonic is the angle of Miguel, and the invariant $K$ does not depend on the inclination, so the angle does not fix $K$; the $K$ that the posted note of 1 eV would require is recorded, $" + _g405(_ev405.get("K_si_para_u_posto_J_s2")) + r"$ J/s$^2$, not chosen. \textsf{[ONTO]} The disk as a psionic condensate is the operator's reading.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Observer = terminal.} \textsf{[REAL]} In a finite model whose levels are position labels (the stone asserts nothing about the human observer, gravity or light as entities), on the kernel's four-level cascade: the terminal is the level \texttt{gravidade} alone; the resistance is consumed at each reading and vanishes only at the terminal; rereading at the terminal adds nothing; the fusion is the collapse, and the collapse is a posted One of the kernel: it paid a loss (the function is not injective) and was measured before being posted (\emph{measured} is the field of the type \texttt{UmPosto}: before $\neq$ after); with the pair 1=1 $|$ 1=0 the fixed points of the collapse are exactly the post and the abyss; the terminal reads 1 and the abyss reads 0 on the binary reading (\texttt{the\_fixed\_points\_read\_one\_and\_zero}); without the abyss the fusion would read as presupposed. Beside it, the $\omega$ pole of the pair reads 1 on the identity (\texttt{the\_omega\_pole\_reads\_one}). \textsf{[ONTO]} A homonym, said aloud: there \emph{terminal} is a pole of the pair $\alpha/\omega$, here it is the level of the cascade; no term links the two, and linking them is the operator's reading. The engineering reading, the collapse as the terminal point of the resistance of the structure, is the operator's.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The stone Identity.} \textsf{[REAL]} The stone proves a fact about projections in the normalized trace state: $\mathrm{tr}(1)/n=\mathrm{tr}(P)/n$ iff $P=1$ iff ($P=(\mathrm{tr}(P)/n)\cdot1$ and $P\neq0$); the void ($P=0$) and the face ($\tfrac12(1+\Gamma)$) do not satisfy the equation. The calculation checks " + _i405(_iv405.get("n_nomes")) + r" names. \textsf{[ONTO]} That this fact \emph{is} the identity is the operator's reading, typed as a model. The name is his. His essay comes in the next section.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The Great Attractor.} \textsf{[DECISION of the management c1, by the operator's order]} The class of the Great Attractor test changed, alongside, from \texttt{A3\_APOSENTADO} to \texttt{A13\_FORMA\_CONDICIONAL\_SEM\_INCERTEZA} (record \texttt{ga\_reclassificacao\_v405}; exit iii of DELIVERY 005), because the audit measured the failure of the extension to the galactic branch, not an error in the mass of the Great Attractor: the form stays alive and conditional on the source bridge, the radial law and the admissibility of the edge; the window keeps its veto, is not evidence and does not discriminate from GR. The constant, the table row and the sealed audit stay as they are.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Errata alongside (v405).} \textsf{[REAL]} \textbf{E10:} the text of \texttt{neutrino\_mass.angle\_status} and erratum E7 of v404 stay in the record; the factor $\sin45^\circ$ has two readings that coincide in form (the derivative of the transverse projection and the zero point of the psion), and one more reading of the same $\sin45^\circ$, by arithmetic (\texttt{o\_psion\_e\_a\_projecao\_do\_modo}); and $E_0=u=1$ eV is \textsf{[POSTO]}, neither declared nor derived. \textbf{E11:} the provisional names and the declared status of $E_0$ were true at the date; the operator posted the unit on 31/10 and gave the names on 01/11/2026. \textbf{E12} \textsf{[KNOWN/DECLARED]}\textbf{:} with the total energy, the invariant of the real Euler's disk is $K=6Mg^2$; $4Mg^2$ was the count with the potential energy alone, written in addendum 4 of the handoff and in the stone before erratum R2, which now keeps it alongside; no number for $K$ is chosen by the target. "
             r"\textbf{E13} \textsf{[REAL]}\textbf{:} the management wrote, in the naming receipt and in addendum 6 of the handoff, that the mass chain was left without a hypothesis and that only the posted One and $\alpha$ remained: that claimed too much and was the management's error, in its own name. The fields closed; the readings moved to the definition. Four theorems were renamed before the seal, because the name claimed more than the theorem proves (no proof changed because of that): \texttt{a\_transicao\_existe\_para\_todo\_acoplamento}, \texttt{the\_tonic\_lands\_on\_the\_posted\_unit}, \texttt{the\_tonic\_at\_the\_posted\_one} and \texttt{the\_omega\_pole\_reads\_one}; and the disk gained \texttt{the\_flow\_is\_the\_canonical\_law}. The revisit of the Law of the Diminished, ordered by the operator, corrected three things: the chord was not typed (Kimi's \texttt{AcordeE0.lean} had it); the sentence about the no-go erred both by excess and by default; and the first correction read the second half of the law as a transposition, the management's error: the diminished is a modulation, and \texttt{transpor} is only the freedom of the no-go.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Limits.} \textsf{[OPEN]} The unit $u$ and $\alpha$ are not derived; that the neutrino mass is the quantity $m_2$ is an \textsf{[ONTO]} reading, and what tests it is nature (JUNO), not the kernel; which disk it is; which the five notes are; magnetism in the chain of the tension. No number was chosen by proximity. GR is the classical limit, not a rival, and $\beta$ does not renormalize local $G$. Validity in the kernel is not creditation; the gate does not move. The box ``The Test of the Only Word'' stays at the top, with its $5\sigma$ line.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The closing.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator, on 01/11/2026 (management translation, not a quotation; the Portuguese original is in the Portuguese edition): we are ending where it had to end, deriving the mass and defining the identity; this is the TGL.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Origin.} \textsf{[REAL]} Machine line, read from the core of this rite: sealed base v404 \texttt{" + _V405_CONTRACTS["ponte"]["baseline"]["sha256"][:16] + r"}; records sealed " + ", ".join(k_.replace("_", r"\_") + "=" + ("yes" if (core.get(k_) or {}).get("all_verified") is True else "no") for k_ in _rg405)
             + r"; verdict of the neutrino channel \texttt{" + _tx_405_t((core.get("neutrino_mass") or {}).get("verdict")) + r"} (unchanged).")
    _pa405 = _v405_ensaio_tex(_V405_IDENTIDADE_EN_TXT)
    s.append(r"\section*{" + _pa405[0] + r"}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{" + _pa405[0] + r"}")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Frame of the section.} \textsf{[OPERATOR'S DECLARATION / INPUT; ONTO reading]} The text below, between the two rules, is a translation by the management of the operator's essay: it is not a quotation, and the Portuguese text (in the Portuguese edition) is the one that governs: the r2 revision (the form is by the management c1; the six content decisions are his), ratified by him on 01/11/2026; the original as received is embedded by sha256 (\texttt{" + _V405_ENSAIO_ORIGINAL_SHA16 + r"}). It is not a theorem. The stone \texttt{TGLExt/Identidade} proves a fact about projections in the trace state; that this is the identity is an \textsf{[ONTO]} reading, typed as a model. This caveat stays here, outside his text.")
    s.append(r"\medskip\hrule\medskip")
    s.extend(_pa405[1:])
    s.append(r"\medskip\hrule\medskip")
